# Compiling and resolving: checked spec

What the compiler promises about hashes, the property everything else in a content-addressed
codebase rests on: two programs that mean the same get the same hash, two that differ do not,
and what the printer shows compiles back to what was stored. [CORE.md](CORE.md) defines Core and
its text form; [LANGUAGE.md](LANGUAGE.md) the surface syntax. The process (D92): requirements,
then the APIs and laws, then the evidence in [Laws](#laws). `deus mdl docs/spec/COMPILE.mdl`
checks it.

## Extensions

| Term  | URI                     |
| ----- | ----------------------- |
| `req` | `org.dxos.deus.req@1.0` |
| `api` | `org.dxos.deus.api@1.0` |
| `law` | `org.dxos.deus.law@1.0` |

## APIs

```mdl
api A-1: parsing and batch compilation
  signatures:
  - Compile.parseFile : Text -> Text -> {Throw Text} (Text, List Decl)
  - Compile.batch : Map Text Entry -> (Text -> {Throw Text | e} Option Sexp) -> (Text -> {Throw Text | e} Option Sexp) -> Text -> List (Text, List Decl) -> {Throw Text | e} Batch
  - Resolve.strip : Sexp -> (Sexp, List Text)
  - Resolve.hashFor : Text -> Sexp -> Text
```

## Hashes follow meaning

```mdl
law L-1: renaming a local never changes a hash
  theorem: Compile.Spec.localNamesDoNotChangeHashes
```

```mdl
law L-2: changing what a definition computes changes its hash
  theorem: Compile.Spec.bodiesChangeHashes
```

```mdl
req R-1: comments, doc comments and layout never change a hash (D66)
  by: Compile.Spec.commentsDoNotChangeHashes
```

```mdl
law L-3: the order of definitions in a file and of files in a batch never changes a hash
  theorem: Compile.Spec.orderDoesNotChangeHashes
```

```mdl
req R-2: mutually recursive definitions hash as one cycle, member i addressed as h.i
  by: Tests.mutualRecursionHashesAsCycle
```

```mdl
req R-3: resolution strips local names out of Core into metadata
  by: Tests.resolveStripsNames
```

## Resolution

```mdl
req R-4: a name in a definition resolves in its own namespace first (Lean's rule)
  by: Compile.Spec.namesResolveInTheirNamespace
```

```mdl
req R-5: batch names shadow names of the base namespace
  by: Compile.Spec.batchShadowsBase
```

## Checking

```mdl
req R-6: an ill-typed definition is refused
  by: Compile.Spec.refusesIllTyped
```

```mdl
req R-7: performing an ability a written row does not declare is refused; an arrow without braces constrains nothing
  by: Compile.Spec.refusesUndeclaredAbility
```

```mdl
req R-9: a row written on a definition with no binders is checked
  gap: task a03fdfb6 (LANGUAGE.md notes it is not)
```

## Printing

```mdl
law L-4: printed source compiles back to the same hashes
  theorem: Compile.Spec.printedSourceCompilesBack
```

```mdl
req R-8: every definition of the toolchain prints back to its own hash
  gap: task a2da28e2; the vitest "adds the compiler to a codebase…" in src/cli.test.ts covers it
```

## Declarations without a body

`def parse (t : Text) : Int` with no `:=` declares a definition before it has an implementation
(D93). Callers compile against the signature; running it is a defect.

```mdl
req R-10: a declaration with a full signature and no body compiles, and its callers are checked against the signature
  by: Compile.Spec.declarationsCheckCallers
```

```mdl
req R-11: a declaration needs a result type and a type on every parameter
  by: Compile.Spec.refusesIncompleteDeclarations
```

```mdl
req R-12: calling a declaration raises the defect "not implemented: <name>"
  by: Compile.Spec.declarationsRaiseADefect
```

```mdl
law L-5: a declaration's hash covers its name, so two declarations alias only when they share name and type
  theorem: Compile.Spec.declarationsHashTheirName
```

```mdl
req R-13: a declaration's hash covers its type, and differs from any implementation
  by: Compile.Spec.declarationsHashTheirType
```

```mdl
req R-14: a declaration prints without a body and compiles back to its hash, also after it is renamed
  by: Compile.Spec.printedSourceCompilesBack | Compile.Spec.renamedDeclarationsRoundTrip
```

```mdl
req R-15: an api block reports a declared name as a known gap, not a failure
  by: Compile.Spec.apiReportsDeclarationsAsGaps
```

```mdl
req R-16: updating a declaration with an implementation rehashes its callers, which then run it
  by: Compile.Spec.implementingRehashesCallers
```

## Laws

The sources compile against a small prelude of builtin types, so they need no codebase.

```deus
namespace Compile.Spec

def prelude : Text :=
  "inductive Int @\"#Int\" where\ninductive Text @\"#Text\" where\ninductive Unit @\"#Unit\" where\n  | unit\ninductive Bool @\"#Bool\" where\n  | false\n  | true\n"

/-- Compiles files after the prelude; the entries in name order, or the error. -/
def compileFiles (files : List Text) : Result Text (List (Text, Entry)) :=
  match try (fun _ =>
    Compile.batch Map.empty (fun _ => none) (fun _ => none) "strict" (List.mapIndexed (fun i f => Compile.parseFile ("f" ++ Int.toText i ++ ".deus") f) (prelude :: files))) with
  | Result.ok b => Result.ok (Map.toList (Map.fromList b.entries))
  | Result.err message => Result.err message

def hashOf (source : Text) (name : Text) : Option Entry :=
  match compileFiles [source] with
  | Result.ok entries => List.lookup name entries
  | Result.err _ => none

def refused (source : Text) : Bool :=
  match compileFiles [source] with
  | Result.ok _ => false
  | Result.err _ => true

/-- Identifiers to rename with, chosen by a generated number, since generated text is rarely an identifier. -/
def local (i : Int) : Text := Option.getOr (List.get? ["x", "y", "n", "value", "acc", "x2", "fooBar", "k_1"] (i % 8)) "x"

theorem localNamesDoNotChangeHashes (i : Int) (j : Int) :
    hashOf ("def f (" ++ local i ++ " : Int) (" ++ local j ++ "z : Int) : Int := " ++ local i ++ " + " ++ local j ++ "z\n") "f" =
      hashOf "def f (a : Int) (b : Int) : Int := a + b\n" "f" := by test 64

theorem bodiesChangeHashes (k : Int) :
    (hashOf ("def f (a : Int) : Int := a + " ++ Int.toText k ++ "\n") "f" == hashOf "def f (a : Int) : Int := a + 7\n" "f") = (k == 7) := by test 64

test commentsDoNotChangeHashes :=
  let plain := hashOf "def f (a : Int) : Int :=\n  let b := a + 1\n  b * 2\n" "f"
  Option.isSome plain &&
    plain == hashOf "-- lead\n/-- Doubles one more. -/\ndef f (a : Int) : Int :=\n  -- a note\n  let b := a + 1\n  b * 2 -- trailing\n" "f" &&
    plain == hashOf "def f (a : Int) : Int :=\n    let b := a + 1\n    b * 2\n" "f"

/-- Two definitions, one using the other, compiled in every order and split. -/
def orderAgnostic (k : Int) : Bool :=
  let a := "def a (n : Int) : Int := b n + " ++ Int.toText k ++ "\n"
  let b := "def b (n : Int) : Int := n * 2\n"
  compileFiles [a ++ b] == compileFiles [b ++ a] && compileFiles [a, b] == compileFiles [b, a] && compileFiles [a ++ b] == compileFiles [b, a]

theorem orderDoesNotChangeHashes (k : Int) : orderAgnostic k = true := by test 16

test namesResolveInTheirNamespace :=
  match compileFiles ["def one : Int := 1\nnamespace N\ndef one : Int := 2\ndef two : Int := one + one\nend N\ndef three : Int := one + N.two\n"] with
  | Result.ok entries =>
    let inner := hashOf "def one : Int := 2\ndef two : Int := one + one\n" "two"
    Option.isSome inner && List.lookup "N.two" entries == inner
  | Result.err _ => false

test batchShadowsBase :=
  match try (fun _ =>
    let first := Compile.batch Map.empty (fun _ => none) (fun _ => none) "strict" [Compile.parseFile "a.deus" (prelude ++ "def k : Int := 1\ndef user : Int := k\n")]
    let base := Map.fromList first.entries
    let second := Compile.batch base (fun h => List.lookup h first.objects) (fun h => List.lookup h first.metas) "strict" [Compile.parseFile "b.deus" "def k : Int := 2\ndef user : Int := k\n"]
    (List.lookup "user" first.entries, List.lookup "user" second.entries, hashOf "def k : Int := 2\ndef user : Int := k\n" "user")) with
  | Result.ok (before, after, expected) => before != after && after == expected
  | Result.err _ => false

test refusesIllTyped := refused "def f : Int := \"x\"\n" && refused "def g (a : Int) : Text := a\n" && not (refused "def h (a : Int) : Int := a\n")

/-- A written row is closed (`{}` is pure); an arrow without braces has a fresh row and constrains nothing. -/
test refusesUndeclaredAbility :=
  let abilities := "ability A where\n  op : Int -> Int\nability B where\n  other : Int -> Int\n"
  refused (abilities ++ "def f (u : Unit) : {} Int := A.op 1\n") &&
    refused (abilities ++ "def f (u : Unit) : {B} Int := A.op 1\n") &&
    not (refused (abilities ++ "def f (u : Unit) : {A} Int := A.op 1\n")) &&
    not (refused (abilities ++ "def f (u : Unit) : Int := A.op 1\n"))

/-- Every program here prints back to the hashes it compiled to. -/
def roundTrips : List Text :=
  ["def f (a : Int) : Int := if a == 0 then 1 else a * 2\n",
    "inductive Shape @\"urn:spec:Shape\" where\n  | circle (r : Int)\n  | rect (w : Int) (h : Int)\ndef area (s : Shape) : Int :=\n  match s with\n  | Shape.circle r => 3 * r * r\n  | Shape.rect w h => w * h\n",
    "structure P @\"urn:spec:P\" where\n  x : Int\n  y : Int\ndef moved (p : P) : P := { p with x := p.x + 1 }\n",
    "ability Ask where\n  ask : Int -> Int\ndef twice (u : Unit) : {Ask} Int := Ask.ask 1 + Ask.ask 2\ndef answered (u : Unit) : Int :=\n  handle twice () with\n  | return v => v\n  | Ask.ask n -> k => k (n * 10)\n",
    "def even (n : Int) : Bool := if n == 0 then true else odd (n - 1)\ndef odd (n : Int) : Bool := if n == 0 then false else even (n - 1)\n",
    "def s : Text := \"tab\\tquote\\\"\\u{1F600}\"\ndef g (a : Int) : Int :=\n  let h := fun (b : Int) => b + a\n  h (h a)\n",
    "test t := 1 + 1 == 2\ntheorem th (b : Bool) : (if b then b else b) = b := by decide\n",
    "/-- Parses a number. -/\ndef parse (t : Text) : Int\ndef k : Int\ndef twice (t : Text) : Int := parse t * k\n"]

theorem printedSourceCompilesBack (i : Int) :
    Codebase.Spec.inStore (fun dir =>
      let source := Option.getOr (List.get? roundTrips (i % List.length roundTrips)) ""
      let first := Compile.batch Map.empty (fun h => Codebase.readObject dir h) (fun h => Codebase.readMeta dir h) "strict" [Compile.parseFile "a.deus" (prelude ++ source)]
      Codebase.store dir first
      let ns := Map.fromList first.entries
      let printed := Text.join "\n\n" (List.map (fun pair => Cli.viewEntry dir ns (fst pair) (snd pair) false) first.entries)
      let again := Compile.batch Map.empty (fun h => Codebase.readObject dir h) (fun h => Codebase.readMeta dir h) "strict" [Compile.parseFile "b.deus" printed]
      Map.toList (Map.fromList again.entries) == Map.toList ns) = true := by test 24

test declarationsCheckCallers :=
  let parse := "def parse (t : Text) : Int\n"
  not (refused (parse ++ "def twice (t : Text) : Int := parse t * 2\n")) &&
    refused (parse ++ "def wrong (t : Text) : Text := parse t\n") && refused (parse ++ "def wrong (n : Int) : Int := parse n\n")

test refusesIncompleteDeclarations :=
  refused "def f (a) : Int\n" && refused "def f (a : Int)\n" && refused "def f\n" &&
    not (refused "def f (a : Int) : Int\n") && not (refused "def k : Int\n") && not (refused "def f (a b : Int) : {} Int\ndef g : Int := 1\n")

/-- Adds `source` after the prelude to the simulated codebase `cb`. -/
def addSource (source : Text) (isUpdate : Bool) : {IO, Throw Text} Unit :=
  IO.mkdirp "src"
  IO.writeFile "src/a.deus" (if isUpdate then source else prelude ++ source)
  Export.Spec.deus "cb" ["src"] (fun a => Cli.addOrUpdate a isUpdate)

def verdictText (name : Text) : {IO, Throw Text} Text :=
  let ns := Codebase.current "cb"
  match Map.lookup name ns with
  | some e =>
    match Check.verdictOf "cb" ns e with
    | some (Verdict.pass _ _) => "pass"
    | some (Verdict.fail reason) => reason
    | _ => "none"
  | none => "none"

test declarationsRaiseADefect :=
  Codebase.Spec.inStore (fun _ =>
    addSource "def parse (t : Text) : Int\ntest usesParse := parse \"1\" == 1\n" false
    Text.startsWith "defect: not implemented: parse" (verdictText "usesParse"))

theorem declarationsHashTheirName (i : Int) (j : Int) :
    (hashOf ("def " ++ local i ++ " (a : Int) : Int\n") (local i) == hashOf ("def " ++ local j ++ " (a : Int) : Int\n") (local j)) = (local i == local j) := by test 64

test declarationsHashTheirType :=
  let declared := hashOf "def f (a : Int) : Int\n" "f"
  Option.isSome declared && declared != hashOf "def f (a : Int) : Text\n" "f" && declared != hashOf "def f (a : Text) : Int\n" "f" &&
    declared != hashOf "def f (a : Int) : Int := a\n" "f" && declared == hashOf "def f (b : Int) : Int\n" "f"

test renamedDeclarationsRoundTrip :=
  Codebase.Spec.inStore (fun dir =>
    addSource "def parse (t : Text) : Int\n" false
    Export.Spec.deus "cb" ["parse", "read"] (fun a => Cli.mv a false)
    let ns := Codebase.current "cb"
    match Map.lookup "read" ns with
    | some e =>
      let printed := Cli.viewEntry "cb" ns "read" e false
      let again := Compile.batch ns (fun h => Codebase.readObject "cb" h) (fun h => Codebase.readMeta "cb" h) "strict" [Compile.parseFile "b.deus" printed]
      not (Text.contains "def read (t : Text) : Int\n" (printed ++ "\n")) && List.lookup "read" again.entries == some e
    | none => false)

test apiReportsDeclarationsAsGaps :=
  Codebase.Spec.inStore (fun _ =>
    addSource "def parse (t : Text) : Int\ndef twice (t : Text) : Int := parse t * 2\n" false
    let ns := Codebase.current "cb"
    let api := fun (line : Text) => Cli.withHost "cb" ns (fun _ => Spec.checkApi (Block.mk "api" "A-1" "t" [("signatures", line)] 0))
    api "parse : Text -> Int" == ["gap: parse is declared but not implemented"] && api "twice : Text -> Int" == [] &&
      api "parse : Text -> Text" == ["parse has type Text -> Int, the spec says Text -> Text"])

test implementingRehashesCallers :=
  Codebase.Spec.inStore (fun _ =>
    addSource "def parse (t : Text) : Int\ndef twice (t : Text) : Int := parse t * 2\ntest usesParse := twice \"1\" == 4\n" false
    let before := Map.lookup "twice" (Codebase.current "cb")
    let failed := verdictText "usesParse"
    addSource "def parse (t : Text) : Int := 2\n" true
    before != Map.lookup "twice" (Codebase.current "cb") && Text.contains "not implemented" failed && verdictText "usesParse" == "pass")

end Compile.Spec
```
